MSR JSON — authorship
=====================

Author and creator of the protocol
----------------------------------
Antonio Santos
  Esplanada, Bahia, Brazil
  snarthost@gmail.com

Antonio Santos designed and wrote the MSR JSON specification, the JSON Schemas,
the reference manifests and the RFC series, and is the author of the Craft
Engine framework.

Attribution
-----------
The specification is licensed CC-BY-4.0 (see LICENSE-SPEC). Attribution is a
condition of that license: any implementation, quotation, translation or
derivative of the specification must credit Antonio Santos as its author.

Stewardship
-----------
Authorship and stewardship are separate on purpose. The protocol is authored by
one person and stewarded in the open: the RFC process, the compatibility policy
and the neutrality charter at https://msrjson.org/governance/ govern how it
changes. No commercial entity controls the specification, and implementing it
requires no permission, fee or registration.
